WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.413
Please welcome, everybody, Jean.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.686
Okay, Jean.

3
00:00:05.686 --> 00:00:08.853
(audience applauding)

4
00:00:10.736 --> 00:00:15.540
Just walk us through exactly what happened, please.

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.840
I was doing the crossroad puzzle,

6
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.230 line:15%
texting with my son when the house phone rings.

7
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:24.930 line:15%
I answer the house phone and it's a person crying

8
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.930 line:15%
saying that he's in an accident and that he's in jail.

9
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.560 line:15%
First I thought it was my son-in-law fooling around,

10
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.220 line:15%
then when he called me grandma, I realized it was a scammer.

11
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.260 line:15%
And so I played along with the scenario,

12
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.950 line:15%
I asked him, "where are you?"

13
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:41.970 line:15%
He said, "I'm in Jersey."

14
00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.710 line:15%
I said, "what are you doing in Jersey?"

15
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.610 line:15%
I played along.

16
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.680 line:15%
He gave me a case number and a phone number to call

17
00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.970
to speak to somebody in the municipal court about,

18
00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:54.930
you know, what he had to do next, he had to get a lawyer.

19
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.557
And before I hung up with him, I said,

20
00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.600
"listen, don't call your mother.

21
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.080
She'll be mad, let me handle this."

22
00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.350
And I think that's what kind of reeled him in,

23
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.810
just me acting like I was really going to fall for this,

24
00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.360
and that's what happened.

25
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.430
And then I had gotten a lawyer,

26
00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.130
and now the lawyer is calling me back,

27
00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.467
Matt Levine his name is, and he says to me,

28
00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:19.960
"well, it's $8,000 in bail, can you handle that?"

29
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.867
And I said to him,

30
00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:25.630
"just so happens that I'm having my kitchen replaced

31
00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.840
and the cabinets are coming next week

32
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.880
and I have $8,000 in the house."

33
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.746
I never thought he'd fall for it, he fell for it.

34
00:01:32.746 --> 00:01:33.980
(audience applauding)

35
00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:37.420
So I tell him I have $8,000 in the house,

36
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.090
and then that's when it really started to get busy.

37
00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:44.530
He knew where I was, he knew how old I was,

38
00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.080
and he's telling me he has to find a bail bondsman now.

39
00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.550
By then, my son knows I'm still on the phone with them.

40
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.370
He's calling my daughters,

41
00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.490
one's a federal officer and the other one works at 911,

42
00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.347
and he's telling them,

43
00:01:56.347 --> 00:01:58.830
"do you know what your mother's doing?"

44
00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:02.386
And you also were a former 911 operator?

45
00:02:02.386 --> 00:02:04.710
Yes, yes, yes, in Nassau County.

46
00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:08.900
Okay, what did you feel when you knew

47
00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.770
they knew your home address?

48
00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.810
Then I was, okay, my daughters are right.

49
00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:13.820
I should call the police.

50
00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.050
I should at least get them here to file a report.

51
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.700
And then all of a sudden, the bail bondsman is in Massapequa

52
00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.500 line:15%
which is 10 minutes from my house,

53
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.620 line:15%
and he says he'll be there in less than 10 minutes.

54
00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:27.650 line:15%
I look at the two cops taking the report, they look at me,

55
00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:29.830
their cars are parked in front of the house.

56
00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:32.030
They ran out the door, got in their cars,

57
00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.700
took 'em down to the firehouse and got back to the house,

58
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.650
and in under 10 minutes, he was there to pick up the money.

59
00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.630
Now, where are the cops now?

60
00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.170
Well, now they're telling me what to do.

61
00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.080
You know, before,

62
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.690
none of us thought it was gonna really happen.

63
00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:46.810
Now they're telling me, "just walk to the door,

64
00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.330
read him the numbers that he's asking you to read,

65
00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.510
and then just step out of the way."

66
00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.797
And that's what I did.

67
00:02:52.797 --> 00:02:55.964
(audience applauding)

68
00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.780
In that 10 minutes, I was a little worried.

69
00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:00.990
That was the only time.

70
00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.800
When I really knew they were coming, I was worried for me,

71
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.970
I was worried for these two young cops

72
00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.310
that had to come there,

73
00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:09.470
and I didn't even want the bad guy to get hurt.

74
00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.020
I didn't want any shots fired,

75
00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:12.543
I wanted it to go down textbook, and it did.

76
00:03:12.543 --> 00:03:16.337
I love it, You're just like, yep, got you.

77
00:03:17.326 --> 00:03:18.950
(audience applauding)

78
00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.960
Oh my God, look, they all come running out.

79
00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.280
I know.

80
00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.700
What advice do you have

81
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.713
for anybody else who may receive a similar call?

82
00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.593
Just hang up, mostly.

83
00:03:34.579 --> 00:03:37.950
People ask me if I would do it again, I don't know.

84
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.633
It was a little bit of fun.

85
00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.530
Well, you're so tough as nails

86
00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:48.530
and the town of Hempstead wanted to honor your bravery

87
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.283
and they have something for you, so take a look.

88
00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.300 line:15%
Hi, I'm Hempstead Supervisor, Don Clavin.

89
00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.530 line:15%
And Jean, we just wanna say thank you.

90
00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:59.730 line:15%
I'm Councilman Chris Carini and we're honored to give you

91
00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.220 line:15%
a Hometown Hero Award.

92
00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.340
On behalf of the 750,000 residents

93
00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.910
here in the town of Hempstead, we want to say great job.

94
00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.279
Thank you.

95
00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:09.220
Thank you.

96
00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:14.220
And we have an official proclamation here for you.

97
00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:20.530
And maybe hang this up somewhere near your landline

98
00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:26.800
so that every day you can know you're everyone's hero.

99
00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.270
And I can't thank you enough for coming

100
00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:32.800
on this show and telling us your story because it does have

101
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.370
a really rock-solid, baller, happy ending.

102
00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.620
And it's all attributed to you.

103
00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.680
Thank you for having me.

104
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.263
(upbeat music)

